# Specification Quality Checklist: Meeting-Room Bookings

**Purpose**: Validate specification completeness and quality before proceeding to planning
**Created**: 2026-11-10
**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md)

## Content Quality

- [x] No implementation details (languages, frameworks, APIs)
- [x] Focused on user value and business needs
- [x] Written for non-technical stakeholders
- [x] All mandatory sections completed

## Requirement Completeness

- [x] No [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers remain
- [x] Requirements are testable and unambiguous
- [x] Success criteria are measurable
- [x] Success criteria are technology-agnostic (no implementation details)
- [x] All acceptance scenarios are defined
- [x] Edge cases are identified
- [x] Scope is clearly bounded
- [x] Dependencies and assumptions identified

## Feature Readiness

- [x] All functional requirements have clear acceptance criteria
- [x] User scenarios cover primary flows
- [x] Feature meets measurable outcomes defined in Success Criteria
- [x] No implementation details leak into specification

## Notes

- Items marked incomplete require spec updates before `/speckit-clarify` or `/speckit-plan`
- Validation ran once; no item needed a second iteration.
- "No implementation details", "Written for non-technical stakeholders" and "No implementation details leak" pass with a stated reading, not literally: the feature description itself fixes routes, status codes, error codes, header names, the queue name, the one-transaction rule and the split of duties between gateway, `booking`, `room` and `worker`. The spec keeps those verbatim as required external behaviour and constraints (FR-001 to FR-025, FR-033) and adds no technical choice of its own: no framework, library, table, class or file is named.
- SC-007 names the repository's build, lint and test commands because the description's "Done when" does; the other success criteria are free of technology names.
- No [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers were raised. Points the description left open were decided with the simplest option and recorded under Assumptions; the ones most worth a second look in `/speckit-clarify` are: overlapping bookings are accepted, a queue failure after storing leaves the booking `PENDING` with no recovery, and a key reused with a different body answers 422 even while the first request is in progress.
import 'reflect-metadata';
import { DataSource } from 'typeorm';
import { DatabaseEnvDto, databaseEnvSchema } from '../config/database-env.schema';
import { RoomEntity } from '../entities/room.entity';
import { migrations } from './migrations';

const { error, value } = databaseEnvSchema.validate(process.env, { allowUnknown: true });
if (error) {
  throw new Error(`Invalid database configuration: ${error.message}`);
}
const env: DatabaseEnvDto = value;

export const dataSource = new DataSource({
  type: 'postgres',
  host: env.DB_HOST,
  port: env.DB_PORT,
  username: env.DB_USERNAME,
  password: env.DB_PASSWORD,
  database: env.DB_DATABASE,
  entities: [RoomEntity],
  migrations,
  synchronize: false,
});
import { CreateRooms1731200000000 } from './1731200000000-create-rooms';
import { SeedRooms1731200000001 } from './1731200000001-seed-rooms';

export const migrations = [CreateRooms1731200000000, SeedRooms1731200000001];
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ConfigService } from '@nestjs/config';
import { TypeOrmModuleOptions, TypeOrmOptionsFactory } from '@nestjs/typeorm';

@Injectable()
export class TypeOrmConfigService implements TypeOrmOptionsFactory {
  constructor(private readonly config: ConfigService) {}

  createTypeOrmOptions(): TypeOrmModuleOptions {
    return {
      type: 'postgres',
      host: this.config.getOrThrow<string>('DB_HOST'),
      port: this.config.getOrThrow<number>('DB_PORT'),
      username: this.config.getOrThrow<string>('DB_USERNAME'),
      password: this.config.getOrThrow<string>('DB_PASSWORD'),
      database: this.config.getOrThrow<string>('DB_DATABASE'),
      autoLoadEntities: true,
      synchronize: false,
    };
  }
}
import { Controller, Get, Inject } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ClientProxy } from '@nestjs/microservices';
import { HealthStatusDto, NATS_CLIENT, NatsRequestUtil } from '@roombook/backend-common';
import { ApiRouteEnum, HealthPatternEnum, ServiceNameEnum } from '@roombook/contract';

@Controller(ApiRouteEnum.HEALTH)
export class HealthController {
  constructor(@Inject(NATS_CLIENT) private readonly client: ClientProxy) {}

  @Get(ServiceNameEnum.BOOKING)
  booking(): Promise<HealthStatusDto> {
    return this.check(HealthPatternEnum.BOOKING);
  }

  @Get(ServiceNameEnum.ROOM)
  room(): Promise<HealthStatusDto> {
    return this.check(HealthPatternEnum.ROOM);
  }

  @Get(ServiceNameEnum.WORKER)
  worker(): Promise<HealthStatusDto> {
    return this.check(HealthPatternEnum.WORKER);
  }

  private check(pattern: HealthPatternEnum): Promise<HealthStatusDto> {
    return NatsRequestUtil.send<HealthStatusDto, Record<string, never>>(this.client, pattern, {});
  }
}

